sources.description:
GPS must report a geographical position; Bluetooth home/away cannot identify an outdoor zone. A room sensor should have its matching local home/away guard. Wearing is optional and cannot be inferred from not charging. Manual sources require checking their meaning in preview.

Suggested sources (confirm which physical device each belongs to):
{suggestions}

geocoding.description:
Rooms, Home, zones and Away work without an account. Optional address descriptions send fresh outdoor coordinates for people you enable to the shared service. Rooms and known zones take precedence.

{service}

Configure the household service once, then enable it separately for each person. Changing the shared service affects everyone already enabled. Settings apply only after final Save.

lookup_geoapify.description:
[Get an API key from Geoapify](https://myprojects.geoapify.com/). Paste it below; no service URL is needed.

{saved_key}

The field is masked. The key is stored privately in Home Assistant configuration, not encrypted by this integration. It is shared only within your HA installation and sent to Geoapify for lookup. Never post it in bug reports or chat.

